course: dictionary
lesson: 13216
title: Fussiness: being hard to please
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fussiness is a noun. It means being fussy: hard to please, worrying about small things, or wanting everything done in a very particular way. Someone who is fussy shows fussiness.
explain: Most often, fussiness is about food. «Mia's fussiness about food meant she would only eat plain pasta.» Mia refuses lots of foods, so fussiness here means being picky about what you eat.
explain: Fussiness can also mean worrying too much about small details, or having too many decorations. «The teacher's fussiness over tiny spelling mistakes meant the project took all week.» The clues are tiny details and all week: the teacher cared too much about small things.
fact: Fussiness is a noun, so you can say «her fussiness» or «the fussiness of the room».
fact: Fussiness means being hard to please, especially about food, clothes or how things are done.
fact: Fussiness can also mean worrying too much about small details.
fact: In art and design, fussiness means too much decoration, so something looks busy and fiddly.
fact: Useful phrases: «fussiness about food», «a fussy eater», and «without fussiness», which means simple and plain.
exercise: «Mia's fussiness about food meant she would only eat plain pasta.» What does fussiness mean here? | Being very fast at cooking | Eating food in a loud way | Liking to swim in the sea | *Being hard to please about food
exercise: «The teacher's fussiness over tiny spelling mistakes meant the project took all week.» What does fussiness mean here? | Painting bright pictures | Forgetting the homework | *Worrying too much about small details | Being kind to every child
exercise: «The cake had so much icing and sugar flowers that its fussiness spoiled it.» What does fussiness mean here? | *Having too much decoration, so it looks busy | Having no decoration at all | Being very cold to touch | Tasting of lemons
test: Which phrase from the lesson means a child who is picky about food? | A tidy room | A loud whistle | *A fussy eater | A bright sunny day
test: «Without fussiness, the garden was simple: a few plants and a bench.» What does without fussiness suggest? | Covered in paint | *Without too much decoration or worry over small things | With lots of tiny flowers | With a huge, busy design
exam: Which sentence uses fussiness correctly? | The river had a loud fussiness of rain | *Ravi's fussiness meant he checked that every sock matched before he left | The sun had a bright fussiness in the sky | The dog's fussiness was a long run in the park
